{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And they shall make.</b> Because he said at first 'and they shall make for Me,' he began thus: 'and they shall make an ark.'" "And we do not know whether this measure is outer or inner. Now if it is outer, the thickness of the ark overlaid within and without on both sides will be half a cubit, so that the measure of each Tablet of the Covenant will be one cubit length and one cubit width. And if we say that the height too is half a cubit, each stone will be very heavy. Perhaps HaShem gave great strength to the hands of Moses, for they were heavy to bring down a stone tablet in one hand. And it is written 'on their two sides' (below, 15) — perhaps it was so, for the tablet is a cubic body that has six faces. And thus it is written that there were three arks, and one may wonder at the weight; and further, for the thickness of the kapporet is one handbreadth; and further, for we have seen that the gold of the waving was only less than one part out of three thousand four hundred of the gold that David set aside. Now the cherubim were of olive wood; also the altar of incense was not entirely gold. And it stands to reason that the overlaying is for the appearance of the eye, and a little gold suffices for overlaying — behold, for the planks, the bars, the table, and the altar of incense are all overlaid, and nothing is entirely gold except the Menorah. And after they made the ark of gold, what need is there for wood? And the overlaying is proved by this: behold, the hall and the house, Solomon overlaid with gold."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:17.706874551Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}